WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.920
STEPHANIE WONG:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.940
about game-changing automation
with GKE, BigQuery BI Engine,

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.037
and keeping the Cloud safe.

00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:10.620
I'm Stephanie Wong, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:14.080
we serve you the
lowest-latency news.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.500
Organizations that need the
highest levels of reliability,

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.860
security, and scalability
for their applications

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.130
choose Google Kubernetes
Engine, or GKE.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.920
Until now, Kubernetes
still involved a fair bit

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.910
of manual assembly and tinkering
to optimize it for your needs.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.840
We're introducing GKE
Autopilot, a revolutionary mode

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.600
of operations for
managed Kubernetes that

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.650
lets you focus on your software
while GKE Autopilot manages

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:44.650
the infrastructure, like
autoscaling and auto-upgrades

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.610
of nodes plus Day 2 operations.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.360
We're also extending
BigQuery BI Engine

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.330
to work with any business
intelligence or custom

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.610
dashboarding
applications that require

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.250
sub-second query response times.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.070
In this preview, BI Engine
will work seamlessly

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.680
with Looker and other
popular BI tools

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.310
without requiring any change
to the BI tools themselves.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.160
Not only is BI Engine
now natively integrated

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.870
into the BigQuery API.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:16.500
You can also reserve BI Engine
capacity in your own GCP

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.370
project.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.950
Check out the announcement
for more info.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.740
This podcast will bring
you stories and insights

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.720
on security in
the Cloud and what

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.780
we're doing at Google
Cloud to help keep customer

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.490
data safe and workloads secure.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.270
We'll do our best to cut to
the heart of real security

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.800
questions and issues.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.230
If you have topics you're
interested in hearing about,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.340
listen to the podcast
and let us know.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:43.730
Need a quick overview of
Google Cloud Core Technologies?

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:47.630
Quickly learned these 21 Google
Cloud products from Anthos

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.440
to Pub/Sub, each explained
in under two minutes.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.960
Check out the blog to read
more and see the videos.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.360
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.130
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.650
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.730
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.350
We'll see you in the Cloud.

